Version: 0.5.8.3
Description:
	My Course Library: the learner's own courses, presented as four independent datasets - current,
	completed, favourites and requests - each in its own accordion with its own paginated table and
	its own live search.

	Four tabs holding four unbounded arrays came before this. Each was filtered in PHP after the
	whole set had been loaded, so the page grew with the learner's history and no list ever said
	how much it was not showing. Every dataset here is counted and paged in the database.

	The accordion, the table, the search control and the pagination control are all the shared
	platform ones, identical to the Company and Administration screens. Nothing on this page is a
	variant built for it.

	The first accordion is open on arrival so the page is not a wall of closed bars; the rest are
	closed. All four are rendered by the server in one request, so no section can be left empty by
	a theme that supplies its own page wrapper.

	WARNING: a template comment is not a safe place to document syntax. Keep every comment plain
	prose: no angle brackets, no comment delimiters and no template tokens, not even as an example.
Changelog:
	2026/08/31 19:05 SAST
	- Round: shared search button moved into noscript, server-search marker on every results region, Course Library rebuilt as paginated accordions, Reports paginated and searched, company requests as a table, company dashboard Courses figure.
	2026/08/31 16:20 SAST
	- Rebuilt from four tabbed card lists into four accordions of paginated, searchable tables.
